{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:545bd476eeb3359d","name":"HX2 Antipersonnel Mine","source":{"id":"source:reference-545bd476eeb3359d","title":"HX2 Antipersonnel Mine","revision":21619,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:09:24Z","sha256":"5f90d2f3cd0d35998d87984908df443326c6fa3b851984affc922783d905e7ef","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21619","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=HX2%20Antipersonnel%20Mine&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-545bd476eeb3359d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Wars Miniatures Previews"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Wars_Miniatures_Previews"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 750\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 1 Kilogram\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Conner Ship Systems HX2 Antipersonnel Mine was popular with ",{"tag":"a","children":["ARC Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/ARC_Troopers"}," during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", and it is still in widespread use during the Galactic Civil War a generation later. It has a powerful adhesive disc that allows it to be attached easily to walls, underneath ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", and so forth. There are two ways to deploy the HX2 Mine: Carefully emplaced using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," skill, or dropped or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"}," a short distance. If carefully emplaced (a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},"; see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Handle Explosives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Handle_Explosives"},"), the Mine can also be hidden (",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," check, adding +15 size modifier of the Mine) to reduce the likelihood that it is detected by enemy infantry.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Mine arms itself 6 seconds later, at the end of your next turn. The Mine will detonate if it detects a target within 1 square (",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +10). Make an attack roll (1d20+10) against the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of every creature and object in the blast radius. (Any creature or object to which the Mine is attached is hit automatically.) If the attack succeeds, the creature or object takes full damage. If the attack misses, the creature or object takes half damage.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If dropped (a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},") or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"}," (a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},"), no ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check is necessary. However, the Mine is less accurate (attack roll 1d20+0), and it will not arm itself until it detects no targets within 1 square. This built-in safety feature makes the Mine useless as an improvised ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grenade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grenade"},", but it does prevent premature detonation. A dropped or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"}," HX2 Antipersonnel Mine can be detected with a successful DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Small\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 6d6 (Energy)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 4-Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
